<title>UK: Profit-taking sends Zeneca lower.</title>
<headline>Profit-taking sends Zeneca lower.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares Zeneca fell 27-1/2 pence to 1,722-1/2 on profit-taking after its recent strong performance.</p>
<p>The drugs firm earlier reported a 14 percent rise in nine-month sales, in line with analysts' expectations.</p>
<p>&quot;It's just profit-taking,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>The share price has been fuelled by persistent takeover rumours this year, hitting a year closing high of 1,758 on October 21. The price eased back slightly afterwards only to advance 11 pence on Monday.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
